## Mock Setup Patterns

### 1. Service Method Mocking
```java
// For methods returning data
Mockito.when(this.[service].[method](parameters)).thenReturn(expectedData);

// For void methods
Mockito.doNothing().when(this.[service]).[method](parameters);

// For methods throwing exceptions
Mockito.when(this.[service].[method](parameters))
    .thenThrow(new [Exception]("Error message"));
```

### 2. APIResponder Mocking
**CRITICAL**: Controllers use the 4-parameter version of `apiResponder.respond()` method. Tests must match the exact method signature used in the controller.

```java
// For successful responses with data (when service returns data)
Mockito.when(this.apiResponder.respond(eq(expectedData), eq(Messages.SUCCESS_MESSAGE), eq(APIResponseType.SUCCESS), eq(HttpStatus.OK)))
    .thenReturn(expectedResponseEntity);

// For successful responses without data (when service returns void) - MUST use <Void> generic type
Mockito.when(this.apiResponder.<Void>respond(null, Messages.SUCCESS_MESSAGE, APIResponseType.SUCCESS, HttpStatus.CREATED))
    .thenReturn(expectedResponseEntity);

// For error responses
Mockito.when(this.apiResponder.respondWithError("Error message", HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST))
    .thenReturn(errorResponseEntity);
```

**CRITICAL**: Use correct 4-parameter pattern based on controller implementation:
- ✅ **Service returns data**: `this.apiResponder.respond(data, "message", APIResponseType.SUCCESS, HttpStatus.OK)` (4 parameters)
- ✅ **Service returns void**: `this.apiResponder.<Void>respond(null, "message", APIResponseType.SUCCESS, HttpStatus.CREATED)` (4 parameters with <Void> generic)
- ❌ **Incorrect**: `this.apiResponder.respond(data, "message")` (2 parameters - doesn't match controller)
- ❌ **Incorrect**: `this.apiResponder.respond(null, "message")` (2 parameters - doesn't match controller)

**HTTP Status Codes by Operation**:
- **CREATE operations**: `HttpStatus.CREATED` (201)
- **GET/UPDATE/DELETE operations**: `HttpStatus.OK` (200)
- **CLONE operations**: `HttpStatus.CREATED` (201)

**Required Imports for 4-Parameter Pattern**:
```java
import io.recruitcrm.microservice.timesheet.responses.APIResponseType;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
```

## Assertion Patterns

### 1. Response Verification
```java
// Verify response entity
assertThat(response).isEqualTo(expectedResponseEntity);

// Verify response status
assertThat(response.getStatusCode()).isEqualTo(HttpStatus.OK);

// Verify response body
assertThat(response.getBody()).isEqualTo(expectedResponse);
```

### 2. Mock Verification
```java
// Verify service method calls
Mockito.verify(this.[service]).[method](parameters);

// Verify API responder calls (4-parameter version)
Mockito.verify(this.apiResponder).respond(expectedData, Messages.SUCCESS_MESSAGE, APIResponseType.SUCCESS, HttpStatus.OK);

// Verify API responder calls for void operations (with <Void> generic)
Mockito.verify(this.apiResponder).<Void>respond(null, Messages.SUCCESS_MESSAGE, APIResponseType.SUCCESS, HttpStatus.CREATED);

// Verify method called with specific parameters
Mockito.verify(this.[service]).[method](eq(expectedParameter));

// Verify method never called
Mockito.verify(this.[service], never()).[method](any());
```

